---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { email, duniaVideo } from "../../data.js";
---

<Base
  title="Dunia"
  description="Dunia is an SDK that captures gameplay at engine level and turns it into labelled training data for AI and robotics teams."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap page">
      <span class="eyebrow">AI division</span>
      <h1>Dunia</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        An SDK that captures gameplay at engine level and turns it into labelled training data for AI and
        robotics teams.
      </p>

      <div class="video" style="margin-top:32px">
        <iframe src={duniaVideo.embed} title="Dunia demo video" allow="autoplay; fullscreen" allowfullscreen></iframe>
      </div>
      <p class="caption">
        The Dunia SDK MVP running in our demo game.
        <a href={duniaVideo.link} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the video</a>
      </p>

      <h2>The problem</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        Robots and world models learn from interaction data: the state of the world, what the agent did, and
        what happened next. Real-world robot data is slow and expensive to collect, and sometimes it breaks
        the robot. Data with the actions labelled barely exists on the web.
      </p>

      <h2>How Dunia works</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The SDK hooks into the game engine and records state, inputs and outcomes as the player acts.</li>
        <li>It takes a snapshot at each decision point, so the data follows choices rather than every tick.</li>
        <li>Every step comes out labelled, because the engine already knows the state and the action.</li>
        <li>The export format is set by the buyer.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Where it is today</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        A working MVP of the SDK runs inside our own demo game. That is what the video shows. The next
        version gets built alongside the first teams who use it, so it solves a real problem for them.
      </p>

      <h2>Who it is for</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Robotics and physical AI teams who need interaction data.</li>
        <li>Data companies who buy and resell training data.</li>
        <li>Game studios who want to put the SDK in their own game.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn main" href={`mailto:${email}?subject=Dunia%20pilot`}>Talk to us about a pilot</a>
        <a class="btn" href={`mailto:${email}?subject=Dunia%20SDK%20for%20my%20game`}>Put Dunia in your game</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
